  "history": "This expressway is being built on a completely new path from the Varanasi Ring Road to the edge of Kolkata, crossing four states. Today the same journey on the old Grand Trunk Road route can take 12 hours or more; the expressway is expected to cut that roughly in half. Work is under way in Uttar Pradesh, Bihar and Jharkhand, while the West Bengal stretch has moved slower because of disputes over the route, so completion is now expected around 2028.",
  "facts": [
    "About 610 km long, crossing Uttar Pradesh, Bihar, Jharkhand and West Bengal.",
    "A greenfield expressway that runs south of the old Grand Trunk Road (NH 19) route.",
    "Part of the Bharatmala highway-building programme.",
    "Expected to cut Varanasi–Kolkata travel time roughly in half, to about 6–7 hours.",
    "Ends on NH 16 near Uluberia, on the outskirts of Kolkata."
  ],
